      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-3x+2 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x+11\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x+\\,\\,2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we conclude the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"140\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11$</td>\n\n<td width=\"20\" align=\"center\">$=$</td>\n\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"120\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30\" align=\"center\">$+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"50\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"25\" align=\"left\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"140\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$x+1$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"50\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$x+1$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-3x+2 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x+11\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x+\\,\\,2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11$ by the linear binomial $x+1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $4{x}^{2}-3x+2,$ and\n\n- the remainder $9.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11}{x+1}=4{x}^{2}-3x+2+\\frac{9}{x+1}.\n$$",
